    <!--
        Rooted, not merely referenced. ILC analyses what is reachable, so a probe that only
        constructs a few types proves those few types AOT-clean and says nothing about the rest —
        the assembly could be full of reflection nobody called from here. Rooting each assembly asks
        ILC to compile every method in it, which is the question actually being asked: "is this
